[   17.748] What went wrong
[   17.748] Immucore checks the OS image against the sha256 recorded for it
[   17.750] before it mounts it, and the check did not pass.
[   17.750] 
[   17.750]   Problem:
[   17.750]     stale checksum: the image changed since it was recorded
[   17.750]   Image:
[   17.750]     /sysroot/run/initramfs/cos-state/cOS/active.img
[   17.751]   Expected sha256 (stored in active.img.sha256):
[   17.752]     fb868208d29bbd110048e09557719803b62807d82977543841942d3e3b443b85
[   17.752]   Actual sha256 (computed from the image just now):
[   17.752]     (not available)
[   17.752] 
[   17.752]   The checksum file describes an older image (size or modification time
[   17.753]   differ), so it cannot vouch for this one. The image was not read.
[   17.753] 
[   17.754]   Action: fail (from image-checksum.conf on the state partition)
[   17.755]   A missing or stale checksum is a problem too: require is on
[   17.755]   (from image-checksum.conf on the state partition)
[   17.755] 
[   17.755] How to fix
[   17.755]   - Reboot and pick the passive or recovery entry in the boot menu.
[   17.756]     Then repair the image with kairos-agent upgrade or reset.
[   17.758]   - To boot this image anyway, edit the boot entry (press e) and add
[   17.758]     image-checksum.verify=warn to the kernel line.
[   17.758]   - A disk that corrupts images can corrupt more: check its health.
[   17.758] 
